# ============================================================================
# CONFIDENTIAL SOURCE MATERIAL — deliberately not published
# ============================================================================
# These are the client's own materials and are excluded by default because a
# repository's visibility cannot be assumed:
#
#   Pitch deck.pdf   marked "DRK / CONFIDENTIAL" on every page
#
# Everything the build needs is already committed — the transcribed content
# lives in `interactive-deck/content/drk.ts` and the derived object plates in
# `interactive-deck/public/brand/objects/`.
Pitch deck.pdf

# demo.mp4 is NO LONGER excluded. It ships as `interactive-deck/public/demo.mp4`
# so scene 10 can play it, on the client's explicit instruction and with the
# repository's PUBLIC visibility confirmed at the time of the decision. It is a
# recording of the live application on mainnet and shows real pool, wallet and
# execution values. Treat it as published: it is in public git history and is
# served unauthenticated from the deployed deck.

# --- source media masters ---------------------------------------------------
# NOT ignored. `demo final.mp4` (the client's raw screen recording, 42MB) is
# tracked through Git LFS — see .gitattributes. Git carries a pointer; LFS
# carries the binary. Its deploy-sized, chaptered outputs at
# interactive-deck/public/demo/ are ordinary Git objects and remain what ships.
